    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0854" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg750"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The only account of this meeting that has been found is in Arnold, <ref
                        target="#pg473">p. 473</ref>, which indicates that Marshall took a poll of
                    the opinion of officers present as to when each of them thought the war with
                    Germany would be ended. The place of the meeting is not given; the time of the
                    meeting is inferred from Arnold’s account and from the Log, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg660">p. 660</ref>.</p>
                <p>TUESDAY, DECEMBER 7, 1943<anchor n="1" xml:id="d458-f1"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d458-f1" n="1" xml:id="d458-f1-content">
                <p>For a post-Conference report of a Steinhardt-Vyshinsky conversation and an
                    Eden–Vyshinsky conversation at Cairo after Roosevelt had departed, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">see post</hi>, <ref target="#pg858">pp. 858</ref>–<ref
                        target="#pg859">859</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
